      "text": "First, identify the rectangular coordinates of the point given:\n$$\n\\begin{align*}\nx &= 0 \\\\\ny &= -3 \\sqrt{3} \\\\\nz &= 3\n\\end{align*}\n$$\nNext, we use the following formulas to convert from rectangular coordinates to spherical coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{align*}\n\\rho &= \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2 + z^2} \\\\\n\\theta &= \\arctan\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right) \\\\\n\\phi &= \\arccos\\left(\\frac{z}{\\rho}\\right)\n\\end{align*}\n$$\n\nApplying these formulas, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{align*}\n\\rho &= \\sqrt{(0)^2 + (-3 \\sqrt{3})^2 + 3^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{0 + 27 + 9} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{36} \\\\\n&= 6\n\\end{align*}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $\\theta$, we use the tangent function. Since the point lies in the third quadrant,\n\n$$\n\\begin{align*}\n\\theta &= \\arctan\\left(\\frac{-3 \\sqrt{3}}{0}\\right) \\\\\n&= \\arctan\\left(-3 \\sqrt{3}\\right) \\\\\n&= \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} - \\pi \\\\\n&= -\\frac{\\pi}{2}\n\\end{align*}\n$$\n\nWe need to make $\\theta$ positive. Adding $2 \\pi$ to $-\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, we get\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\theta &= \\arccos \\left(\\frac{3}{6}\\right) \\\\\n&= \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}\n\\end{align*}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n$$\n\\begin{align*}\n\\phi &= \\arccos \\left(\\frac{3}{6}\\right) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\pi}{6}\n\\end{align*}\n$$\n\nSo the spherical coordinates for $(0, -3 \\sqrt{3}, 3)$ are\n\n$$\\boxed{\\left(6,\\frac{3 \\pi}{4} , \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right)}.$$.",
