      "text": "To convert from rectangular coordinates to spherical coordinates, we use the following formulas:\n$(\\rho, \\theta, \\phi) = ( \\sqrt{x^2+y^2+z^2}, \\tan^{-1}( y / x ),  \\tan^{-1}(z/\\rho) )$\n\nSo the given point can be converted as follows:\n$\\rho = \\sqrt{0^2 + (-3\\sqrt{3})^2 + 3^2} = \\sqrt{18} = 3 \\sqrt{2}$\n\n$\\theta = \\tan^{-1} (-3\\sqrt{3} / 0) = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\n\n$\\phi = \\tan^{-1}(3/(3 \\sqrt{2})) = \\sqrt{2}$\n\nTherefore, the conversion of the given point from rectangular to spherical coordinates is $\\boxed{(3 \\sqrt{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\sqrt{2})}$.The answer is: (3\\sqrt{2},\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\sqrt{2})",
